1. Definitions

1.1. "Contributor" means a person or entity that creates or supplies Covered Material and authorizes its licensing under this License.
1.2. "Covered Material" means material expressly designated as subject to this License, modifications of that material, and new files containing copyright-protected portions of that material. Independently created files that contain no such portions are not Covered Material solely because they interoperate with it.
1.3. "Source Form" means the preferred editable form of Covered Material, including source code, native design files, schematics, board layouts, mechanical models, documentation, and the associated configuration, build, fabrication and assembly information reasonably necessary to modify and reproduce the distributed material or Covered Product. General-purpose tools, independently licensed dependencies and credentials need not be supplied; necessary dependencies, versions and instructions must be identified, and any material required under this License must be supplied.
1.4. "Non-Source Form" means any representation of Covered Material other than Source Form, including compiled binaries, flattened documents and fabrication exports that are not the preferred editable form.
1.5. "Distribution" means supplying or making copies available to another person or entity. Transfers strictly within a single organization or its controlled affiliates, solely for their internal use, are excluded. Control means the power to direct management or policies, whether by ownership or otherwise.
1.6. "Restricted Commercialization" means supplying Covered Material, or access to its substantial functionality, to third parties in exchange for direct or indirect economic consideration attributable to that supply or access, including sale, rental, subscription, paid hosting, mandatory support, paid feature access, advertising revenue attributable to such access, or inclusion as a material component of a paid product or service. Merely using Covered Material to produce independent goods or services is excluded. The exceptions in Section 3 apply.
1.7. "You" means the person or entity exercising rights under this License.
1.8. "Covered Product" means a physical or digital article made by reproducing or implementing a material portion of a design expressly licensed under this License, including a modified design, or an article materially incorporating Covered Material or such a design. An article does not become a Covered Product merely because a tool governed by this License was used to create it. Independently developed designs, standard components and unrelated articles are not Covered Products merely because they interoperate with Covered Material.
1.9. References to Restricted Commercialization include offering, selling, leasing or otherwise supplying a Covered Product for consideration, whether directly, through an intermediary, or as a material component of a paid offering. Voluntary donations and the express exceptions in Section 3 remain permitted.

